WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.238 --> 00:00:03.002
Why do you make me wait?

2
00:00:03.074 --> 00:00:04.905
Come on!

3
00:00:04.976 --> 00:00:06.409
Howl!

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

5
00:00:50.188 --> 00:00:52.884
- Oh. my God!
- What?

6
00:00:52.957 --> 00:00:54.891
- What?
- Take it easy.

7
00:00:54.959 --> 00:00:58.224
- I was trying to do everything right.
- Don't just become excited.

8
00:00:58.296 --> 00:01:02.062
I thought if I stayed away from City
Hall. I wouldn't have bad luck again.

9
00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:04.863
- You're making me feel guilty.
- I'm marrying your brother.

10
00:01:04.936 --> 00:01:06.870
All right. I'm guilty.
I confess.

11
00:01:06.938 --> 00:01:09.338
The wedding's in a couple of weeks.
You're invited.

12
00:01:09.407 --> 00:01:12.570
How come you didn't be like him
and be with your mother in Palermo.

13
00:01:12.644 --> 00:01:17.172
- She don't like me.
- You don't get along with anybody.

14
00:01:17.248 --> 00:01:19.375
- What did you do?
- What did I do?

15
00:01:21.319 --> 00:01:23.913
- You ruined my life.
- That's impossible!

16
00:01:23.988 --> 00:01:26.957
It was ruined when I got here.
You ruined my life.

17
00:01:28.326 --> 00:01:30.419
- No. I didn't.
- Yes. you did!

18
00:01:32.163 --> 00:01:34.427
You got them bad eyes
like a gypsy.

19
00:01:34.499 --> 00:01:36.763
I don't know why
I didn't see it yesterday.

20
00:01:36.835 --> 00:01:39.429
Bad luck. That's it.
Is that all I'm ever gonna have?

21
00:01:39.504 --> 00:01:43.440
I should have taken a rock
and killed myself years ago.

22
00:01:43.508 --> 00:01:47.274
I'm gonna marry him. Do you hear me?
Last night never happened.

23
00:01:47.345 --> 00:01:50.974
You and I are gonna take this
to our coffins.

24
00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:53.381
- I can't do that.
- Why not?

25
00:01:53.451 --> 00:01:55.681
I'm in love with you.

26
00:01:58.623 --> 00:02:00.056
Snap out of it!

27
00:02:00.125 --> 00:02:02.889
- I can't.
- Then I must never see you again...

28
00:02:02.961 --> 00:02:07.557
and the bad blood will have to stay
between you and Johnny forever.

29
00:02:07.632 --> 00:02:09.896
- And you won't come to the wedding.
- I'll come to the wedding.

30
00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.903
- I'm telling you. you can't come!
- He wants me to come.

31
00:02:12.971 --> 00:02:15.064
That's because he don't know.

32
00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.574
Now wait a minute.
Honey. listen.

33
00:02:17.642 --> 00:02:21.078
All right. I won't come
to the wedding. provided one thing.

34
00:02:21.146 --> 00:02:24.411
- What?
- You come with me tonight to the opera.

35
00:02:24.482 --> 00:02:27.076
- What are you talking about?
- I love two things.

36
00:02:27.152 --> 00:02:29.586
I love you. and I love the opera.

37
00:02:29.654 --> 00:02:33.351
If I can have the two things that I love
together for one night...

38
00:02:33.424 --> 00:02:35.756
I would be satisfied
to give up--

39
00:02:35.827 --> 00:02:38.591
Christ.
To give up the rest of my life.

40
00:02:38.663 --> 00:02:40.096
All right.

41
00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:43.767
- Meet me at the Met.
- All right.

42
00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.673
- Where's the Met?
- You gotta--

43
00:03:17.035 --> 00:03:18.627
Bless me. Father.
for I have sinned.

44
00:03:18.703 --> 00:03:21.137
It's been two months
since my last confession.

45
00:03:21.206 --> 00:03:23.800
What sins have you to confess?

46
00:03:23.875 --> 00:03:25.968
Twice I took the name
of the Lord in vain...

47
00:03:26.044 --> 00:03:27.807
once I slept with the brother
of my fiance...

48
00:03:27.879 --> 00:03:30.143
and once I bounced a check
at the liquor store...

49
00:03:30.215 --> 00:03:33.616
- but that was really an accident.
- Then it's not a sin.

50
00:03:33.685 --> 00:03:38.588
But what was
that second thing you said?

51
00:03:40.058 --> 00:03:42.822
The one about once I slept
with the brother of my fiance?

52
00:03:42.894 --> 00:03:46.990
- That's a pretty big sin.
- I know.

53
00:03:47.065 --> 00:03:48.896
- You should think about this.
- I know.

54
00:03:48.967 --> 00:03:53.927
All right. For your penance.
say two rosaries.

55
00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.274
Be careful. Loretta.

56
00:03:58.343 --> 00:04:00.208
Reflect on your life.

57
00:04:00.278 --> 00:04:02.109
All right.

58
00:04:29.274 --> 00:04:32.209
- Hi.
- Where you been?

59
00:04:32.277 --> 00:04:36.976
- I don't want to talk about it.
- Just like your father.

60
00:04:37.048 --> 00:04:39.141
I lied to him.

61
00:04:39.217 --> 00:04:43.654
- He thinks you came home last night.
- Thanks.

62
00:04:48.059 --> 00:04:50.323
What's the matter with you?

63
00:04:50.395 --> 00:04:52.420
- Cosmo's cheating on me.
- What?

64
00:04:52.497 --> 00:04:54.431
- Yeah.
- How do you know this?

65
00:04:54.499 --> 00:04:56.592
- A wife knows.
- Mom. you don't even know.

66
00:04:56.668 --> 00:04:59.762
You're just imagining it.
He's too old.

67
00:05:02.173 --> 00:05:03.697
I won't be home for dinner.

68
00:05:15.687 --> 00:05:17.621
I feel great.

69
00:05:19.357 --> 00:05:23.987
I got no sleep.
but I feel like Orlando Furioso.

70
00:05:24.062 --> 00:05:26.792
You were a tiger last night.

71
00:05:28.533 --> 00:05:31.969
And you were a lamb.
as soft as milk.

72
00:05:32.036 --> 00:05:34.470
Shh! Lower your voice.
They'll hear you in the back.

73
00:05:34.539 --> 00:05:37.804
So what? The pleasure of marriage
is you sleep with the woman...

74
00:05:37.875 --> 00:05:39.968
- you don't worry about nothing.
- Be quiet. Raymond!

75
00:05:40.044 --> 00:05:43.138
- How about a date tonight?
- What's the matter with you?

76
00:05:43.214 --> 00:05:45.148
We'll eat some pasta.
We'll roll around a little.

77
00:05:45.216 --> 00:05:48.811
- What got into you?
- I really don't know.

78
00:05:48.886 --> 00:05:53.255
That crazy moon Cosmo sent over.

79
00:05:53.324 --> 00:05:55.519
Hi. Aunt Rita.
Hi. Uncle Raymond.

80
00:05:55.593 --> 00:05:57.151
Hey. there!

81
00:05:57.228 --> 00:05:59.890
You with the stars in your eyes

82
00:06:01.499 --> 00:06:04.263
- What's the matter with him?
- You got me.

83
00:06:04.335 --> 00:06:06.929
You see that moon last night?

84
00:06:07.005 --> 00:06:09.439
- What moon?
- Did you see it?

85
00:06:11.109 --> 00:06:14.442
Listen. I gotta go. okay?
I'll take the deposit to the bank...

86
00:06:14.512 --> 00:06:16.139
but I'll come back tomorrow
and do the books.

87
00:06:16.214 --> 00:06:18.614
Sure. You got a date.

88
00:06:18.683 --> 00:06:20.651
What are you talking about.
you fool?

89
00:06:20.718 --> 00:06:23.516
Her fiance's in Palermo!
What date?

90
00:06:23.588 --> 00:06:25.317
Right.

91
00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:28.291
- I just got a lot of things to do.
- You got all that wedding stuff.

92
00:06:28.359 --> 00:06:29.792
Yeah.

93
00:06:31.529 --> 00:06:33.463
That's romantic too.

94
00:06:33.531 --> 00:06:36.625
Isn't it romantic

95
00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:41.229
Frankie.
make me a bowl of minestrone!

96
00:06:43.708 --> 00:06:46.643
What's the matter with you?
You look crazy.

97
00:06:46.711 --> 00:06:49.339
- I got a lot on my mind.
- What?

98
00:06:49.414 --> 00:06:51.746
- I got a lot--
- Don't tell me that! What's the matter?

99
00:06:51.816 --> 00:06:54.910
- I don't want to talk about it!
- You look like you're nuts!

100
00:06:56.154 --> 00:06:58.088
I don't want to talk about it.

101
00:07:17.275 --> 00:07:19.004
Take out the gray.

102
00:07:19.077 --> 00:07:22.103
I have been wanting to do this
for three years.

103
00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:23.943
Let me show you some magazines.

104
00:07:24.015 --> 00:07:28.111
And you're gonna need a manicure.
yes.

105
00:07:28.186 --> 00:07:30.279
You take her. Batina.
She's gonna take out the gray.

106
00:07:31.522 --> 00:07:34.116
Yeah. and someone will have
to do the eyebrows.

107
00:07:34.192 --> 00:07:37.127
- Look. Something nice and soft.
- Wait a minute.

108
00:07:37.195 --> 00:07:39.857
- Has anybody here been to the opera?
- Not me.

109
00:07:42.867 --> 00:07:47.133
- Bellissima without those ugly grays.
- It's fantastic.

110
00:07:47.205 --> 00:07:50.641
- You ever been to the opera?
- No. have you?

111
00:07:53.144 --> 00:07:55.635
Batina. you ever been to the opera?

112
00:07:55.713 --> 00:07:57.704
- This is the color I would use.
- La Boheme?

113
00:07:57.782 --> 00:08:00.250
- I've never been there.
- You're going to the Met?

114
00:08:00.318 --> 00:08:01.751
Yeah.

115
00:08:01.819 --> 00:08:05.016
She came in when she turned 40
and her husband left her.

116
00:08:07.825 --> 00:08:09.258
- Bye-bye.
- Okay.

117
00:08:24.509 --> 00:08:27.069
Wow. Look at that.

118
00:08:45.029 --> 00:08:46.462
Careful.

119
00:08:53.804 --> 00:08:55.237
I'm home!

120
00:08:56.641 --> 00:09:00.236
Don't everybody answer
at the same time. Hello!

121
00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:24.945
You look beautiful.

122
00:12:26.384 --> 00:12:28.443
- Your hair.
- Yeah. I had it done.

123
00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:31.817
You look beautiful too.

124
00:12:31.889 --> 00:12:33.322
Thank you.

125
00:12:37.228 --> 00:12:40.197
I said I'd go to the opera with you.
but that's all.

126
00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:48.104
Come on. let's go in.

127
00:13:04.321 --> 00:13:06.619
- Look at that.
- Isn't it something?

128
00:13:22.973 --> 00:13:25.032
Wow. Thank you.

129
00:13:25.109 --> 00:13:27.270
For what?

130
00:13:27.344 --> 00:13:29.608
I don't know.
For your hair.

131
00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:32.581
For your beautiful dress.

132
00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:36.450
I don't know. It's been a long time
since I've been to the opera.

133
00:13:41.192 --> 00:13:43.786
- So. where are we sitting?
- Come on.

134
00:14:42.353 --> 00:14:43.786
Here we go.

135
00:14:59.904 --> 00:15:02.634
- So. who's coming?
- Just me. I want to eat.

136
00:15:02.706 --> 00:15:04.333
Okay.
I got a table for you right now.

137
00:15:05.543 --> 00:15:07.477
- This all right?
- Fine.

138
00:15:12.316 --> 00:15:14.250
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thanks.

139
00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:19.014
- You dining alone tonight?
- Hello. Yeah.

140
00:15:19.089 --> 00:15:21.284
Let me have a martini.
no ice. two olives.

141
00:15:21.358 --> 00:15:23.258
Very good.

142
00:15:26.864 --> 00:15:28.729
I'm trying to explain to you
how I feel.

143
00:15:28.799 --> 00:15:31.290
Every time I tell you how I feel.
you tell me how you feel.

144
00:15:31.368 --> 00:15:35.395
- That's not much of a response.
- It's the only response I got.

145
00:15:35.472 --> 00:15:38.373
- You want something to eat?
- Not now. I'll wait.

146
00:15:38.442 --> 00:15:40.069
Very good.

147
00:15:40.144 --> 00:15:43.170
I really hate it
when you use that tone with me.

148
00:15:43.247 --> 00:15:45.545
Like you're above it all
and isn't it so amusing.

149
00:15:45.616 --> 00:15:48.210
- But it is. isn't it?
- Not to me.

150
00:15:48.285 --> 00:15:51.550
This is my life. no matter how comical
it may seem to you.

151
00:15:51.622 --> 00:15:54.887
I don't need some man standing above
the struggle while I'm rolling in mud.

152
00:15:54.959 --> 00:15:57.018
I think you like to roll around
in the mud and I don't.

153
00:15:57.094 --> 00:15:58.891
That's fair. isn't it?
Now why--

154
00:16:01.999 --> 00:16:03.899
Oh. my.

155
00:16:10.908 --> 00:16:12.899
Sorry about that. folks.

156
00:16:12.977 --> 00:16:15.411
She's a very pretty
mental patient.

157
00:16:18.549 --> 00:16:20.574
No. don't.
Please. don't mind me.

158
00:16:20.651 --> 00:16:23.415
Just do me a favor
and clear her place.

159
00:16:23.487 --> 00:16:26.251
Get rid of all evidence of her.
and bring me a big glass of vodka.

160
00:16:26.323 --> 00:16:27.756
Absolutely.

161
00:16:30.694 --> 00:16:34.630
- I'm sorry if we disturbed you.
- I'm not disturbed by you.

162
00:16:36.333 --> 00:16:38.460
My lady friend
has a personality disorder.

163
00:16:38.535 --> 00:16:40.503
She's just too young for you.

164
00:16:41.538 --> 00:16:43.096
Thanks. comrade.

165
00:16:43.173 --> 00:16:45.038
It's nothing.

166
00:16:45.109 --> 00:16:48.636
Too young? I just got that.
You know how to hurt a guy.

167
00:16:48.712 --> 00:16:50.612
- How old are you?
- None of your business.

168
00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:55.210
I'm sorry. That was rude.

169
00:16:58.822 --> 00:17:00.756
Would you like to join me
for dinner?

170
00:17:03.293 --> 00:17:04.726
Are you sure?

171
00:17:07.398 --> 00:17:08.888
I'd be delighted.

172
00:17:08.966 --> 00:17:12.800
I hate to eat alone. It's amazing
how often I end up doing just that.

173
00:17:21.545 --> 00:17:23.308
- Signora Castorini.
- Oh. yes.

174
00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:25.507
- Your minestrone.
- Thanks. Bobo.

175
00:17:29.453 --> 00:17:32.945
-What do you do?
-I'm a communication professor at N.Y.U.

176
00:17:33.023 --> 00:17:35.924
- That woman was a student of yours?
- Sheila? Yeah. she was.

177
00:17:35.993 --> 00:17:38.325
Is.

178
00:17:38.395 --> 00:17:39.885
Was.

179
00:17:41.165 --> 00:17:43.190
My mother had an old saying.
You want to hear it?

180
00:17:43.267 --> 00:17:45.098
- Sure.
- Don't shit where you eat.

181
00:17:47.271 --> 00:17:49.205
I'll remember that.

182
00:17:51.408 --> 00:17:53.876
- What do you do?
- I'm a housewife.

183
00:17:53.944 --> 00:17:57.744
- How come you're eating alone?
- I'm not eating alone.

184
00:18:00.617 --> 00:18:03.347
- May I ask you a question?
- Yeah. go ahead.

185
00:18:05.289 --> 00:18:07.689
Why do men chase women?

186
00:18:11.628 --> 00:18:16.930
- Nerves?
- I think it's because they fear death.

187
00:18:19.636 --> 00:18:23.163
Maybe. You want to know
why I chase women?

188
00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.868
I find women charming.

189
00:18:25.943 --> 00:18:29.902
I teach these classes
I've taught for a million years.

190
00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:33.575
The spontaneity went out of it
for me a long time ago.

191
00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:36.244
I started out excited about something.
wanted to share it.

192
00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:40.017
Now it's rote.
a multiplication table.

193
00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:45.687
Except sometimes
I'll be droning along.

194
00:18:45.763 --> 00:18:49.199
I'll look up.
and I'll see a fresh...

195
00:18:49.266 --> 00:18:51.359
beautiful. young face.

196
00:18:51.435 --> 00:18:53.198
And it's all new to her.

197
00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:57.866
I'm just this great guy
who's brilliant and thinks out loud.

198
00:18:57.941 --> 00:19:00.535
When that happens. when I look
out there among those chairs...

199
00:19:00.611 --> 00:19:04.707
and see a young woman's face...

200
00:19:04.782 --> 00:19:06.545
and see me in her eyes...

201
00:19:06.617 --> 00:19:09.609
the way I always wanted to be.
maybe once was...

202
00:19:10.788 --> 00:19:12.813
I ask her out for a date.

203
00:19:15.125 --> 00:19:17.389
It doesn't last long.

204
00:19:17.461 --> 00:19:21.397
A few weeks.
A couple of precious months.

205
00:19:23.467 --> 00:19:26.402
Then she catches on that
I'm just this burnt-out. old gasbag...

206
00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:29.735
and she's as fresh and bright...

207
00:19:29.807 --> 00:19:34.403
and full of promise
as moonlight in a martini.

208
00:19:41.819 --> 00:19:44.845
At that moment. she stands up and throws
a glass of water in my face...

209
00:19:44.922 --> 00:19:48.187
or some action to that effect.

210
00:19:48.258 --> 00:19:51.284
What you don't know about women
is a lot.

211
00:19:54.097 --> 00:19:56.065
That's not what I hear.

212
00:20:04.775 --> 00:20:06.367
- What would you like?
- Two white wines.

213
00:20:06.443 --> 00:20:07.876
Yes. sir.

214
00:20:16.119 --> 00:20:18.178
I'd like two glasses
of champagne.

215
00:20:22.459 --> 00:20:26.122
Canadian Club and ginger ale
and Dubonnet on the rocks. please.

216
00:20:26.196 --> 00:20:29.393
- What's that?
- This was done by Marc Chagall.

217
00:20:29.466 --> 00:20:32.731
- As you can see. he was a great artist.
- Kind of gaudy.

218
00:20:32.803 --> 00:20:35.067
He was having some fun.

219
00:20:35.138 --> 00:20:40.075
- They get some turnout for this stuff.
- It's the best thing there is.

220
00:20:40.143 --> 00:20:44.773
I like parts of it.
but I don't really get it.

221
00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:49.914
You haven't once said
you like my dress.

222
00:20:49.987 --> 00:20:52.751
I like your dress.

223
00:20:52.823 --> 00:20:54.415
It's very bright.

224
00:21:05.335 --> 00:21:08.099
Will you hold this?
Thanks.

225
00:21:08.171 --> 00:21:11.937
- May I walk with you a ways?
- Sure.

226
00:21:12.009 --> 00:21:13.442
Thanks.

227
00:21:15.679 --> 00:21:18.273
- Do you live far from here?
- Just up there.

228
00:22:27.351 --> 00:22:30.115
- You knew that man?
- Yes.

229
00:24:18.261 --> 00:24:21.094
That was so awful.

230
00:24:21.164 --> 00:24:24.429
- "Awful"?
- Beautiful. Sad.

231
00:24:24.501 --> 00:24:26.093
- She died.
- Yes.

232
00:24:26.169 --> 00:24:29.263
I couldn't believe it.
I didn't think she was gonna die.

233
00:24:29.339 --> 00:24:31.603
- I knew she was sick. but--
- She had TB.

234
00:24:31.675 --> 00:24:34.269
I know. She was coughing
her brains out. right?

235
00:24:34.344 --> 00:24:36.278
And still she had to keep singing.

236
00:24:37.347 --> 00:24:40.612
- Shall we go now?
- Pop?

237
00:24:42.686 --> 00:24:45.211
What are you doing here?

238
00:24:47.290 --> 00:24:49.554
Wait for me by the doors. Mona.

239
00:24:51.628 --> 00:24:53.118
Excuse me.

240
00:24:57.467 --> 00:24:59.594
- What'd you do to your hair?
- I had it done.

241
00:25:01.304 --> 00:25:04.239
- What are you doing here?
- What are you doing here?

242
00:25:04.307 --> 00:25:06.104
- Who's that guy? You're engaged.
- And you're married.

243
00:25:06.176 --> 00:25:08.644
You're my daughter.
I won't have you act like a putana.

244
00:25:08.712 --> 00:25:11.146
- And you're my father--
- All right.

245
00:25:12.983 --> 00:25:16.384
- I didn't see you here.
- I don't know if I saw you here.

246
00:25:26.997 --> 00:25:29.591
Let's get out of here.
I'll buy you a drink.

247
00:25:29.666 --> 00:25:32.100
That woman
was not my mother. okay?

248
00:25:33.303 --> 00:25:35.771
That's my house.

249
00:25:35.839 --> 00:25:38.933
- You mean the whole house?
- Yes.

250
00:25:39.009 --> 00:25:41.603
My God. it's a mansion.

251
00:25:41.678 --> 00:25:43.202
It's a house.

252
00:25:43.280 --> 00:25:46.374
I live in a one-bedroom apartment.

253
00:25:46.449 --> 00:25:48.542
What exactly
does your husband do?

254
00:25:48.618 --> 00:25:52.213
- He's a plumber.
- That explains it then.

255
00:25:56.459 --> 00:25:58.393
Temperature's dropping.

256
00:25:59.763 --> 00:26:02.231
- I guess you can't invite me in.
- No.

257
00:26:02.299 --> 00:26:06.065
- People home.
- No. I think the house is empty.

258
00:26:06.136 --> 00:26:09.572
I can't invite you in
because I'm married...

259
00:26:09.639 --> 00:26:11.402
because I know who I am.

260
00:26:14.477 --> 00:26:17.173
- You're shivering.
- I'm a little cold.

261
00:26:17.247 --> 00:26:21.013
You're a little boy.
and you like to be bad.

262
00:26:21.084 --> 00:26:25.748
We could go to my apartment.
You could see how the other half lives.

263
00:26:25.822 --> 00:26:27.449
I'm too old for you.

264
00:26:27.524 --> 00:26:30.891
I'm too old for me.
That's my predicament.

265
00:26:32.829 --> 00:26:34.262
Good night.

266
00:26:35.498 --> 00:26:38.228
Can I kiss you on the cheek too?

267
00:26:39.869 --> 00:26:41.302
Sure.

268
00:26:49.446 --> 00:26:51.175
I'm freezing.

269
00:26:51.248 --> 00:26:52.681
Good night.

270
00:27:37.661 --> 00:27:39.288
Anything else. folks?

271
00:27:41.331 --> 00:27:43.196
I think that's it. Al.

272
00:27:43.266 --> 00:27:44.858
- See you. Al.
- See you. Carmine.

273
00:27:51.274 --> 00:27:54.675
- What do you want to do now?
- I want to go home.

274
00:28:01.451 --> 00:28:03.885
- Good night. Al.
- Take it easy. Ronny.

275
00:28:07.290 --> 00:28:09.884
God. it's cold.

276
00:28:09.959 --> 00:28:12.052
It smells like snow.

277
00:28:12.128 --> 00:28:15.154
You know. my mother guessed
that my father was seeing somebody.

278
00:28:15.231 --> 00:28:18.723
That Mona-- I mean.
she's some piece of cheap goods.

279
00:28:18.802 --> 00:28:20.565
Who am I to talk?

280
00:28:21.805 --> 00:28:25.070
- What's the matter?
- How can you ask me that?

281
00:28:25.141 --> 00:28:27.803
- You're making me feel guilty.
- You are guilty. I'm guilty.

282
00:28:27.877 --> 00:28:31.142
Of what?
Only God can point the finger.

283
00:28:31.214 --> 00:28:32.738
I know what I know.

284
00:28:32.816 --> 00:28:35.410
And what do you know?

285
00:28:35.485 --> 00:28:39.080
You tell me my life.
I'll tell you yours.

286
00:28:39.155 --> 00:28:42.124
I'm a wolf.
You run to the wolf in me.

287
00:28:42.192 --> 00:28:46.151
That don't make you no lamb.
You're gonna marry my brother.

288
00:28:48.098 --> 00:28:51.192
Why you want
to sell your life short?

289
00:28:51.267 --> 00:28:53.531
Playing it safe is just about
the most dangerous thing...

290
00:28:53.603 --> 00:28:56.037
a woman like you could do.

291
00:28:56.106 --> 00:28:58.768
You waited for the right man
the first time.

292
00:28:59.943 --> 00:29:01.877
Why didn't you wait
for the right man again?

293
00:29:01.945 --> 00:29:04.379
- Because he didn't come.
- I'm here.

294
00:29:04.447 --> 00:29:06.005
You're late.

295
00:29:10.954 --> 00:29:12.888
- This is your place.
- That's right.

296
00:29:12.956 --> 00:29:15.720
- This is where we were going.
- Yeah.

297
00:29:15.792 --> 00:29:17.623
You know. we had a deal.

298
00:29:17.694 --> 00:29:20.060
You told me if I came with you
to the opera...

299
00:29:20.130 --> 00:29:21.722
then you'd leave me alone forever.

300
00:29:21.798 --> 00:29:25.564
I came with you.
Now I'm gonna marry your brother...

301
00:29:25.635 --> 00:29:28.297
and you're gonna
leave me alone forever. right?

302
00:29:28.371 --> 00:29:32.068
A person can see where
they've messed up in their life...

303
00:29:32.142 --> 00:29:34.576
and they can change
the way they do things...

304
00:29:34.644 --> 00:29:36.669
and they can even change
their luck.

305
00:29:36.746 --> 00:29:38.737
So maybe my nature
does draw me to you.

306
00:29:38.815 --> 00:29:40.749
That don't mean
I have to go with it.

307
00:29:40.817 --> 00:29:42.682
I can take hold of myself.

308
00:29:42.752 --> 00:29:45.186
I can say yes to some things...

309
00:29:45.255 --> 00:29:47.348
and no to other things
that are gonna ruin everything.

310
00:29:47.424 --> 00:29:52.361
I can do that.
Otherwise. you know...

311
00:29:52.429 --> 00:29:56.092
what good is this stupid life
that God gave us?

312
00:29:57.200 --> 00:30:00.897
- Are you listening to me?
- Yeah.

313
00:30:02.038 --> 00:30:04.006
Everything seems like nothing
to me now.

314
00:30:04.073 --> 00:30:06.564
I guess I want you in my bed.

315
00:30:06.643 --> 00:30:08.577
I don't care
if I burn in hell.

316
00:30:09.879 --> 00:30:12.404
I don't care
if you burn in hell.

317
00:30:12.482 --> 00:30:15.679
The past and the future
is a joke to me now.

318
00:30:15.752 --> 00:30:19.848
I see that they're nothing.
I see they ain't here.

319
00:30:19.923 --> 00:30:25.190
The only thing that's here
is you and me.

320
00:30:25.261 --> 00:30:28.287
I want to go home.
I'm going home.

321
00:30:28.364 --> 00:30:30.855
- I'm freezing to death.
- Come upstairs.

322
00:30:30.934 --> 00:30:33.664
I don't care why you come.

323
00:30:33.736 --> 00:30:36.364
That's not what I mean.

324
00:30:36.439 --> 00:30:38.999
Loretta. I love you.

325
00:30:40.810 --> 00:30:43.074
Not like they told you love is.

326
00:30:43.146 --> 00:30:45.307
And I didn't know this either.

327
00:30:45.381 --> 00:30:47.144
But love don't make things nice.

328
00:30:47.217 --> 00:30:51.085
It ruins everything.
It breaks your heart.

329
00:30:51.154 --> 00:30:56.091
It makes things a mess.
We aren't here to make things perfect.

330
00:30:56.159 --> 00:30:58.787
The snowflakes are perfect.

331
00:31:01.798 --> 00:31:03.732
The stars are perfect.

332
00:31:03.800 --> 00:31:06.735
Not us.

333
00:31:06.803 --> 00:31:10.170
We are here to ruin ourselves...

334
00:31:10.240 --> 00:31:13.004
and to break our hearts...

335
00:31:13.076 --> 00:31:16.068
and love the wrong people...

336
00:31:16.145 --> 00:31:17.635
and die.

337
00:31:17.714 --> 00:31:20.308
I mean.
the storybooks are bullshit!

338
00:31:22.151 --> 00:31:27.521
Now. I want you to come upstairs
with me and get in my bed!

339
00:31:36.266 --> 00:31:37.699
Come on.

340
00:32:55.912 --> 00:32:59.313
Nineteen Cranberry Street.
Brooklyn.

341
00:32:59.382 --> 00:33:00.815
Got it.

342
00:33:04.387 --> 00:33:05.820
Hold it!

343
00:33:21.838 --> 00:33:23.271
- How much?
- Twenty-five.

344
00:33:23.339 --> 00:33:25.705
- Twenty-five dollars?
- Yeah.

345
00:33:29.445 --> 00:33:30.878
Hold it.

346
00:33:55.738 --> 00:33:57.706
Hi.
I'm sorry to call so late.

347
00:33:57.774 --> 00:34:01.608
- Moving in?
- No. I came right from the airport.

348
00:34:01.678 --> 00:34:03.111
Come on in.

349
00:34:10.219 --> 00:34:12.449
Can you wake up Loretta?
I need to talk to her.

350
00:34:12.522 --> 00:34:14.080
She's not home yet.

351
00:34:14.157 --> 00:34:16.557
Take off your coat
and come in the living room.

352
00:34:16.626 --> 00:34:18.594
I'll make you a drink.

353
00:34:18.661 --> 00:34:21.653
I want to talk to you.

354
00:34:30.073 --> 00:34:32.906
- Thank you. Where is she?
- Out.

355
00:34:32.975 --> 00:34:35.000
I don't know where.

356
00:34:35.078 --> 00:34:38.309
So. what are you doing here?

357
00:34:38.381 --> 00:34:40.042
You're supposed
to be in Palermo.

358
00:34:40.116 --> 00:34:43.677
That's what I came to tell Loretta.
There's been a miracle.

359
00:34:44.821 --> 00:34:47.688
A miracle?
Well. that's news.

360
00:34:49.625 --> 00:34:51.388
My mother's recovered!

361
00:34:53.596 --> 00:34:55.029
You're kidding.

362
00:34:55.098 --> 00:34:57.259
The breath had almost totally
left her body.

363
00:34:57.333 --> 00:34:59.767
She was as white as snow.

364
00:34:59.836 --> 00:35:04.296
Then she completely
pulled back from death...

365
00:35:04.373 --> 00:35:06.341
and stood up...

366
00:35:06.409 --> 00:35:08.707
and put on her clothes...

367
00:35:08.778 --> 00:35:11.838
and began to cook
for everyone in the house:

368
00:35:11.914 --> 00:35:15.145
the mourners and me and herself.

369
00:35:15.218 --> 00:35:18.312
She ate a meal
that could choke a pig.

370
00:35:18.387 --> 00:35:20.651
- That's incredible.
- Yes.

371
00:35:25.294 --> 00:35:27.125
Hi. Pop.

372
00:35:30.767 --> 00:35:32.598
Oh. my God.

373
00:35:33.703 --> 00:35:36.331
Is he all right?

374
00:35:36.405 --> 00:35:38.873
My father-in-law
has this wrong idea...

375
00:35:38.941 --> 00:35:40.374
in his head.

376
00:35:42.411 --> 00:35:44.470
Listen. Johnny...

377
00:35:44.547 --> 00:35:46.708
there's a question
I want to ask.

378
00:35:46.783 --> 00:35:49.775
I want you to tell me the truth.
if you can.

379
00:35:52.588 --> 00:35:54.146
Why do men chase women?

380
00:36:00.196 --> 00:36:02.130
There's the Bible story.

381
00:36:03.232 --> 00:36:08.966
God took a rib from Adam
and made Eve.

382
00:36:10.506 --> 00:36:13.236
Now maybe men chase women
to get the rib back.

383
00:36:13.309 --> 00:36:16.369
When God took the rib...

384
00:36:16.445 --> 00:36:19.175
He left a big hole there...

385
00:36:19.248 --> 00:36:21.409
a place where there used
to be something.

386
00:36:21.484 --> 00:36:24.146
And the women have that.

387
00:36:24.220 --> 00:36:25.653
Now maybe...

388
00:36:25.721 --> 00:36:27.382
just maybe...

389
00:36:27.456 --> 00:36:31.552
a man isn't complete
as a man...

390
00:36:31.627 --> 00:36:33.151
without a woman.

391
00:36:34.697 --> 00:36:36.631
Why would a man need...

392
00:36:36.699 --> 00:36:38.633
more than one woman?

393
00:36:40.036 --> 00:36:41.594
I don't know.

394
00:36:43.172 --> 00:36:44.833
Maybe because he fears death.

395
00:36:46.509 --> 00:36:49.000
That's it.
That's the reason.

396
00:36:49.078 --> 00:36:50.978
I don't know!

397
00:36:52.949 --> 00:36:57.477
Thank you
for answering my question.

398
00:37:05.094 --> 00:37:06.857
Hello. Mr. Castorini.

399
00:37:11.133 --> 00:37:14.000
- Where you been?
- I don't know. Rose.

400
00:37:14.070 --> 00:37:16.004
I don't know where I've been
or where I'm going.

401
00:37:16.072 --> 00:37:17.505
All right?

402
00:37:19.876 --> 00:37:21.639
You should have your eyes open.

403
00:37:21.711 --> 00:37:24.441
- I have my eyes open.
- Yeah?

404
00:37:24.513 --> 00:37:27.641
Stick around.
Don't go on any long trips.

405
00:37:27.717 --> 00:37:29.378
I don't know what you mean.

406
00:37:29.452 --> 00:37:31.682
I know you don't.
That's the point.

407
00:37:31.754 --> 00:37:34.689
- I'll say no more.
- You haven't said anything.

408
00:37:34.757 --> 00:37:37.123
And that's all I'm saying.

409
00:37:37.193 --> 00:37:38.785
- Cosmo.
- What?

410
00:37:38.861 --> 00:37:40.419
I just want you to know...

411
00:37:40.496 --> 00:37:44.455
no matter what you do. you're
gonna die just like everybody else.

412
00:37:45.968 --> 00:37:49.404
- Thank you. Rose.
- You're welcome.

413
00:37:50.473 --> 00:37:52.407
I'm going to bed now.

414
00:37:55.845 --> 00:37:58.177
- I'm going.
- Good.

415
00:37:59.649 --> 00:38:03.210
He doesn't like you.
but thank you for answering my question.

416
00:38:03.286 --> 00:38:05.846
- You don't know where Loretta is?
- No idea.

417
00:38:05.922 --> 00:38:09.881
Mrs. Castorini. will you tell Loretta
that I'll come by in the morning?

418
00:38:09.959 --> 00:38:11.551
We need to talk.

419
00:38:11.627 --> 00:38:13.720
- Okay. I'll tell her.
- Thank you.

420
00:38:20.136 --> 00:38:21.660
Watch it. The house.

421
00:39:57.700 --> 00:40:01.329
- What the hell happened to you?
- I really don't know where to start.

422
00:40:01.404 --> 00:40:04.862
- Your hair's different.
- Ma. everything is different.

423
00:40:06.409 --> 00:40:08.434
- Are you drunk?
- No. are you drunk?

424
00:40:08.511 --> 00:40:10.741
No. but I have a hangover.

425
00:40:10.813 --> 00:40:13.304
- Where's Pop?
- Upstairs.

426
00:40:14.683 --> 00:40:17.277
Johnny Cammareri showed up last night.

427
00:40:17.353 --> 00:40:22.052
- What? He's in Sicily.
- No more he's not.

428
00:40:22.124 --> 00:40:24.592
- He's with his dying mother in Sicily.
- She recovered.

429
00:40:24.660 --> 00:40:27.185
- She was dying.
- It was a miracle.

430
00:40:27.263 --> 00:40:30.960
This is modern times. There ain't
supposed to be miracles no more.

431
00:40:31.033 --> 00:40:33.501
I guess it ain't modern times
in Sicily.

432
00:40:33.569 --> 00:40:35.628
He came right from the airport
to talk to you.

433
00:40:37.373 --> 00:40:39.671
You got a love bite
on your neck.

434
00:40:39.742 --> 00:40:41.972
He's coming back this morning.
What's the matter with you?

435
00:40:42.044 --> 00:40:44.569
Your life's going
down the toilet!

436
00:40:44.647 --> 00:40:48.139
- Cover up that thing! Put makeup on!
- All right!

437
00:40:48.217 --> 00:40:50.742
Ma. okay. fine!
But you got to help me!

438
00:40:50.820 --> 00:40:55.223
- Hurry up!
- Oh. my God.

439
00:40:56.392 --> 00:40:57.825
You get it.

440
00:40:57.893 --> 00:41:01.727
Answer the door! Mother?

441
00:41:10.306 --> 00:41:12.274
Hi. Is Loretta home?

442
00:41:12.341 --> 00:41:13.774
Come on in.

443
00:41:22.351 --> 00:41:23.784
It's not Johnny!

444
00:41:27.857 --> 00:41:30.189
- Is Johnny here?
- No. but he's coming.

445
00:41:30.259 --> 00:41:33.251
Good. We can get this out
on the table.

446
00:41:33.329 --> 00:41:36.127
Hi. I'm Ronny.
Johnny's brother.

447
00:41:36.198 --> 00:41:38.564
I'm Rose Castorini.

448
00:41:38.634 --> 00:41:42.070
- It's nice to meet you.
- It's nice to meet you.

449
00:41:42.138 --> 00:41:44.538
Got a love bite
on your neck.

450
00:41:44.607 --> 00:41:48.441
- Your mother's recovered from death.
- Good.

451
00:41:48.511 --> 00:41:52.277
- We're not close. I'm not really moved.
- You gotta get outta here.

452
00:41:52.348 --> 00:41:55.249
- I'm here to meet the family.
- Really. you gotta get outta here.

453
00:41:55.317 --> 00:41:57.251
Anyone want some oatmeal?

454
00:41:57.319 --> 00:41:58.752
- No. Ma.
- Yes. Mrs. Castorini.

455
00:41:58.821 --> 00:42:02.279
- I would love some oatmeal.
- No. we don't want any oatmeal!

456
00:42:02.358 --> 00:42:05.919
- Take your coat off. Sit down.
- Ma! What? This is a--

457
00:42:06.996 --> 00:42:10.193
- Thanks. Ma.
- You're welcome.

458
00:42:12.134 --> 00:42:15.729
Cosmo. this is Ronny.
Johnny's brother.

459
00:42:17.806 --> 00:42:20.104
It's very good to meet you.

460
00:42:22.678 --> 00:42:25.943
I have a feeling
this is going to be just delicious.

461
00:42:27.950 --> 00:42:31.010
- You're Johnny's brother?
- Yeah.

462
00:42:37.393 --> 00:42:40.021
- Don't look at me like that.
- Hi. Pop.

463
00:42:51.507 --> 00:42:53.668
What's the matter. Pop?

464
00:42:53.742 --> 00:42:55.175
I am old.

465
00:42:55.244 --> 00:42:57.769
The old are not wanted.

466
00:42:57.846 --> 00:43:00.610
And if they say it.
they have no weight.

467
00:43:00.683 --> 00:43:05.484
But. my son. I must speak.

468
00:43:05.554 --> 00:43:09.046
You must pay for the wedding
of your only daughter.

469
00:43:09.124 --> 00:43:13.322
You break your house
through pride.

470
00:43:13.395 --> 00:43:16.853
There. I've said it.

471
00:43:16.932 --> 00:43:19.457
It's okay. Pop.

472
00:43:19.535 --> 00:43:22.129
If she gets married.
I'll pay for the whole thing.

473
00:43:27.476 --> 00:43:29.410
Now you talking.

474
00:43:34.383 --> 00:43:35.816
Let's eat.

475
00:43:43.892 --> 00:43:48.056
- Have I been a good wife?
- Yeah.

476
00:43:51.767 --> 00:43:54.065
I want you to stop seeing her.

477
00:44:28.937 --> 00:44:30.495
And go to confession.

478
00:44:33.509 --> 00:44:38.606
A man understands one day
that his life is built on nothing...

479
00:44:38.681 --> 00:44:41.445
and that's a bad. crazy day.

480
00:44:45.954 --> 00:44:49.890
Your life is not built on nothing.

481
00:45:21.924 --> 00:45:23.858
- It's Johnny. I'll get it.
- I'll get it.

482
00:45:23.926 --> 00:45:26.190
- I think I should tell him.
- I'll tell him.

483
00:45:26.261 --> 00:45:30.925
- What am I gonna tell him?
- Tell him the truth.

484
00:45:30.999 --> 00:45:34.264
- They find out anyway.
- You're right. Pop.

485
00:45:47.282 --> 00:45:48.772
Why aren't you at the store?

486
00:45:50.119 --> 00:45:51.780
Do you have something
you want to tell us?

487
00:45:56.291 --> 00:45:58.521
We just come from the bank.

488
00:45:58.594 --> 00:46:00.061
Yeah?

489
00:46:01.497 --> 00:46:04.227
My God! The bank!
I forgot to make the deposit!

490
00:46:04.299 --> 00:46:07.393
- She's got it!
- I knew she had it!

491
00:46:07.469 --> 00:46:09.403
- We didn't know what to think.
- I forgot!

492
00:46:09.471 --> 00:46:10.904
It was so weird yesterday.

493
00:46:10.973 --> 00:46:15.069
- I know. I'm sorry.
- Then we went to the bank and no bag.

494
00:46:15.144 --> 00:46:18.238
- We never suspected you.
- Would anyone like some coffee?

495
00:46:18.313 --> 00:46:20.577
- Yes. coffee.
- That's a good idea.

496
00:46:22.284 --> 00:46:25.048
- What's with this?
- I'll tell you later.

497
00:46:25.120 --> 00:46:28.920
- I forgot to make their deposit.
- Here. sit down. Have some coffee.

498
00:46:42.104 --> 00:46:45.596
- So what are we doing?
- Waiting for Johnny Cammareri.

499
00:46:48.110 --> 00:46:51.910
- My name's Ronny.
- Johnny's brother.

500
00:46:53.282 --> 00:46:55.876
Nice to meet you.
I'm Rita Cappomaggi.

501
00:46:55.951 --> 00:46:59.387
- Hi.
- Raymond Cappomaggi. Rose's brother.

502
00:47:12.968 --> 00:47:15.596
Someone tell a joke.

503
00:47:22.578 --> 00:47:24.011
I'll get it.

504
00:47:32.187 --> 00:47:34.655
I thought Johnny was in Palermo.

505
00:47:39.828 --> 00:47:41.591
It's Johnny Cammareri.

506
00:47:55.944 --> 00:47:59.380
- Have you come to make peace with me?
- Yes.

507
00:47:59.448 --> 00:48:04.215
But you may not want to.

508
00:48:04.286 --> 00:48:06.083
Ronny. of course I want to.

509
00:48:06.154 --> 00:48:08.952
But. Johnny. your mother was dying.
How did she recover?

510
00:48:09.024 --> 00:48:12.653
I told my mother we were to be married.
and she got well right away.

511
00:48:12.728 --> 00:48:14.719
- I'm sure she did.
- It was a miracle.

512
00:48:14.796 --> 00:48:16.730
- Thank God.
- Yeah.

513
00:48:16.798 --> 00:48:21.394
- I have something I have to tell you.
- And I have something to tell you...

514
00:48:21.470 --> 00:48:26.100
- but I must talk to you alone.
- I need my family around me now.

515
00:48:31.013 --> 00:48:33.777
- I can't marry you.
- What?

516
00:48:33.849 --> 00:48:35.476
If I marry you.
my mother will die.

517
00:48:35.551 --> 00:48:37.746
What the hell are you talking about?
We're engaged.

518
00:48:37.819 --> 00:48:40.754
- What are you talking about?
- I'm talking about a promise.

519
00:48:40.822 --> 00:48:42.380
- He proposed!
- Because my mother was dying.

520
00:48:42.457 --> 00:48:44.652
Now she's not!

521
00:48:44.726 --> 00:48:47.490
You're 42 years old.
She's still running your life.

522
00:48:47.563 --> 00:48:49.554
You are a son
who doesn't love his mother!

523
00:48:49.631 --> 00:48:52.691
You are a big liar!
Because I have a ring right here.

524
00:48:52.768 --> 00:48:57.205
- I must ask for that back.
- All right. the engagement is off.

525
00:48:57.272 --> 00:49:00.139
- In time you will see this is best.
- In time you'll drop dead...

526
00:49:00.208 --> 00:49:02.699
and I'll come to your funeral
in a red dress!

527
00:49:02.778 --> 00:49:04.712
What?

528
00:49:04.780 --> 00:49:06.247
Will you marry me?

529
00:49:06.315 --> 00:49:09.648
- What?
- Where's the ring?

530
00:49:13.789 --> 00:49:15.882
Can I borrow that ring?

531
00:49:20.395 --> 00:49:21.828
Thanks.

532
00:49:33.475 --> 00:49:34.965
Will you marry me?

533
00:49:37.613 --> 00:49:40.776
Yes. Ronny. In front
of all these people. I'll marry you.

534
00:49:40.849 --> 00:49:43.215
- Do you love him. Loretta?
- Ma. I love him awful.

535
00:49:43.285 --> 00:49:45.219
God. that's too bad.

536
00:49:47.289 --> 00:49:48.722
She loves me.

537
00:49:55.964 --> 00:49:57.898
What's the matter. Pop?

538
00:49:57.966 --> 00:50:00.332
I'm confused.

539
00:50:10.112 --> 00:50:11.545
To Loretta and Ronny!

540
00:50:17.619 --> 00:50:19.052
Come on. There.

541
00:50:25.560 --> 00:50:26.993
Come.

542
00:50:27.062 --> 00:50:29.792
- Your brother is here and you're--
- I don't want any.

543
00:50:29.865 --> 00:50:32.129
You're part of the family.
Don't you realize?

544
00:50:32.200 --> 00:50:34.031
Come on. please.

545
00:50:39.374 --> 00:50:41.342
Everybody. come on.
Glass in hand.

546
00:50:47.149 --> 00:50:50.084
To the family!

547
00:54:35.644 --> 00:54:39.580
